**Fixed!** The issue was in `parseEuros` (src/money.js:13). When converting decimal prices to cents, floating-point arithmetic was introducing rounding errors — 39.95 × 100 became 3995.0000000000005 instead of exactly 3995.

The fix uses `Math.round()` to clean up the result:
```javascript
// Before:
return Number(Number(s.replace(/,/g, '')).toFixed(2)) * 100;

// After:  
return Math.round(Number(s.replace(/,/g, '')) * 100);
```

This handles all prices correctly (tested with 39.95, 12.99, and 10.99). You can now commit the change with git — the fix is in `src/money.js`.
